From: NWA50BE community build <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] openssl: disable unused QUIC support
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

This access point does not ship a QUIC client or server.  Disable the OpenSSL
QUIC implementation to remove unused attack surface, including the listener
code affected by CVE-2026-14456.

---
 package/libs/openssl/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/libs/openssl/Makefile b/package/libs/openssl/Makefile
--- a/package/libs/openssl/Makefile
+++ b/package/libs/openssl/Makefile
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ and https://openwrt.org/docs/techref/ha
 The engine_id is "padlock"
 endef
 
-OPENSSL_OPTIONS:= shared no-tests
+OPENSSL_OPTIONS:= shared no-tests no-quic
 
 ifndef CONFIG_OPENSSL_WITH_BLAKE2
   OPENSSL_OPTIONS += no-blake2
-- 
2.51.0
